     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Energy requirements and energy targets are included in large public buildings.
-A coherent scheme for the implementation of energy management in large existing buildings is implemented.
-Capacity has been strengthened amongst public entities to enhance the regulatory framework regarding energy efficiency in buildings."></target>
     <actual value="Next year report"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Progress in implementing annual activities"></target>
     <actual value="Outcome 3 is not expected to be realised, which was also noted by the MTR. Though the main partner EBTKE has the mandate to establish regulatory framework for energy efficiency, they are currently not considered a strong partner on its own to spearhead substantial advancements in new regulations and enforcement of existing regulatory initiatives. In response, the INDODEPP has adapted its approach to explore opportunities of working with stronger institutions, such as Ministry of Public Works and Ministry of Industry in line with MTR recommendations. A closer dialogue with these institutions is being pursued for 2025 in order to assess the partners&apos; roles, institutional setups, and absorption levels including for the design of the next phase of the Indonesia Denmark energy partnership programme"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
